{"title":"2024 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(arduous_and_not_recommended)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (arduous and not recommended)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by Math-X (First understand the problem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_(Under_3_minutes)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 (Under 3 minutes)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_5_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 5 by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_6_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 6 by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_7_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 7 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_8_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 8 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_9_by_CosineMethod_[Fast_and_Easy]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 9 by CosineMethod [Fast and Easy]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_10_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 10 by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_11_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 11 by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_12_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by 12 WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Effective,_easy_and_simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Effective, easy and simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-24\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Any three vertices of the cube <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/2/b42e9f18df3b09c85ba27cd3bcb2f8114547d9fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRSTUVW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />, shown in the figure below, can be connected to form a triangle. (For example, vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can be connected to form isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.) How many of these triangles are equilateral and contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as a vertex?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc4c5b02dfaf07a435a3a5098a847d0af49d6c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(4); pair P,Q,R,S,T,U,V,W; P=(0,30); Q=(30,30); R=(40,40); S=(10,40); T=(10,10); U=(40,10); V=(30,0); W=(0,0); draw(W--V); draw(V--Q); draw(Q--P); draw(P--W); draw(T--U); draw(U--R); draw(R--S); draw(S--T); draw(W--T); draw(P--S); draw(V--U); draw(Q--R); dot(P); dot(Q); dot(R); dot(S); dot(T); dot(U); dot(V); dot(W); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,NW); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,NW); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,NE); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,S,N); label(&quot;$T$&quot;,T,NE); label(&quot;$U$&quot;,U,NE); label(&quot;$V$&quot;,V,SE); label(&quot;$W$&quot;,W,SW); [/asy]\" width=\"318\" height=\"312\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38f2f5805ba1cca43012a065113e44514187cbdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"349\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The only equilateral triangles that can be formed are through the diagonals of the faces of the square. From P you have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible vertices that are possible to form a diagonal through one of the faces. Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible triangles. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523fe7885d78244830c991d0921da6ff161d8ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />\n~Math645, andliu766, e___\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each other compatible point must be an even number of edges away from P, so the compatible points are R, V, and T. Therefore, we must choose two of the three points, because P must be a point in the triangle. So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578121926d8b7596385310bea046d547bcaf6990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3 \\choose 2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"120\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>-ILoveMath31415926535\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28arduous_and_not_recommended.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(arduous_and_not_recommended)\">Solution 3 (arduous and not recommended)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (arduous and not recommended)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>List them out- you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e587bc47e969473a56a656380b63c1031e50cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PRV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e91fa515b5d0aaf755f6ffbf68cf53d48effd5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PRT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9086b9ccef9729b4f286557b8caaf5119c9363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PVT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4dcb56a890a42e3d22bc2856bc5d88ac3ca76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) 3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"59\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-Anonymussrvusdmathstudent234234\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Easy)\">Solution 4 (Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After looking at the cube, we realize that an equilateral triangle can only be formed by three lines that form a diagonal along a face of the cube (such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb64373ab113ec40ba16bc1e871f0dd7905d58e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PV$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />). Because the problem has a condition that one of the triangle's vertex must be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the three diagonals that can be formed are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da92154963838b99a4a00a094bbb50f22d2287a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PT, PR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb64373ab113ec40ba16bc1e871f0dd7905d58e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PV$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can choose any of 2 out of the 3 lines we have listed, and connect any of them with another line (for example, if we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebdc03b4e24dbee7b5747d6a0aa2def18f5541d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PT$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, the third diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/f/b8fe0bc1f0ab90d60df20bc9e4ccac77d35238e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RT$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />). Thus, there are 3 ways to choose the 3 diagonals, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523fe7885d78244830c991d0921da6ff161d8ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~TechnoDragon\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/OwJvuq6F7sQ\">https://youtu.be/OwJvuq6F7sQ</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/29xcfUcmTgg\">https://youtu.be/29xcfUcmTgg</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_.28Goes_through_full_thought_process.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\">Video Solution 1 by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit s